{title: Annotated}
{artist: Melic}

# "fire" is the classic one: sung as one syllable or two depending on the tune.
{x_melic_word: fire = +fi -re}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
{x_melic_word_section: fire = +fire}
The [Am]fire is out, the [F]night is cold,
A [C]single fire against the [G]dark.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Two [Am]syllables of fire here,
{x_melic_word_line: fire = +fi -re}
And [C]fire again, but slower now.
{end_of_verse}
